# --- Jev API configuration -------------------------------------------------
# Put your real key in .env.local (which is gitignored). Server-side only.

# Your API key. Either name works; JEV_API_KEY takes priority.
JEV_API_KEY=
# AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=

# Which provider issued the key.
# Options: typesafe (direct api.typesafe.ai) | vercel | openrouter | aimlapi
# A direct key that looks like "apikey_..." uses typesafe.
JEV_PROVIDER=typesafe

# Optional overrides (only if you need a custom endpoint / model):
# JEV_BASE_URL=https://api.typesafe.ai/v1/systemone
# JEV_MODEL=jev-latest

# --- API hardening ---------------------------------------------------------
# The /api routes proxy the paid Jev key. By default /api/recommend only accepts
# a KNOWN studentId (the fixed demo cohort), so the public endpoint can't be fed
# unbounded custom payloads to burn the key. Set this to allow arbitrary evidence
# (e.g. for your own authenticated tooling). Leave UNSET for a public deployment.
# ALLOW_CUSTOM_EVIDENCE=1
#
# NOTE: the built-in rate limiter is best-effort per-instance memory. For a real
# public deployment, add auth and a distributed rate limiter / queue in front.
